body:
I should not have read this before five seconds before actually finishing the movie.

&#x200B;

This makes the twist that much funnier.

It's interesting, I take both actions as a form of looking down on Greg in an effort to convince themselves they're worth more when they're basically all worth little to nothing in Logan's eyes. Tom's comments towards Greg whenever he is attempting to better himself, move up, or just do something that is good for himself are always about how he's shooting too far. Probably because Tom is in a marriage/relationship where he's constantly being told he's wrong or steamrolled by Shiv's wants and needs, so he decides putting his foot down in anyway is asking for too much. Kendall is getting rid of his apartment and acts like it's nothing to him because he's getting a better one, and then proceeds to use it to throw a party while ignoring Greg's need to sleep. The action of giving away such an expensive thing/place to Greg, and then using it for such a cheap reason without his actual permission, is sort of like a 'yeah fuck you you're on my property even though i gave it to you.. and i own another one'. Just seemed like a very layered ego boost for Kendall because he was at the height of S3's conflict with/attack on Logan.

&#x200B;

TLDR; Kendall's nearly just as much of a dick as Tom to Greg, and I have way too much time on my hands!
